<body>
<nav><span class="logo">Product Ops · 100 apps</span>
<a href="#headline">Headline</a><a href="#patterns">Patterns</a><a href="#matrix">Matrix</a><a href="#agent">The agent</a>{% if pass3 %}<a href="#pass3">Pass 3</a>{% endif %}<a href="#try">Try it</a><a href="#honesty">Honesty</a><a href="#for-agents">For agents</a></nav>

{% set t = patterns.totals %}
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<span class="tag">Composio · AI Product Ops Intern take-home</span>
<h1>Which of these 100 apps can become an agent toolkit today, and what stands in the way?</h1>
<p>An agent researched every app from its official docs, quoted the page behind each answer, and was checked by verification loops (quote match, Composio's toolkit API, the MCP registry, a second model). Where it could not prove something, it says <b>unknown</b>.</p>
<div class="tiles">
<div class="tile"><b>{{ n }}</b><span>apps researched</span></div>
<div class="tile"><b>{{ t.self_serve_open }}</b><span>self-serve (free or trial)</span></div>
<div class="tile"><b>{{ t.gated }}</b><span>gated (paid, admin, partner, sales)</span></div>
<div class="tile"><b>{{ t.buildable }}</b><span>buildable today (incl. caveats)</span></div>
<div class="tile"><b>{{ t.easy_wins }}</b><span>easy wins not yet in Composio</span></div>
<div class="tile"><b>{{ t.needs_human }}</b><span>rows flagged needs human</span></div>

</div>
</div></header>

<main class="wrap">
<section id="headline">
<h2>Headline</h2>
<p class="sub">Every number below is computed by pandas from the 100 records; {% if patterns.headline.source in ['deterministic','deterministic_fallback'] %}the wording is a fixed template{% else %}the wording is by {{ patterns.headline.source }} and passed a numeric fact-check against those tables{% endif %}.</p>
<div class="card"><ul class="headline">{% for b in patterns.headline.bullets %}<li>{{ b }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% if patterns.headline.rejected_numbers %}<p class="small">The LLM headline was rejected because it used numbers not in the tables ({{ patterns.headline.rejected_numbers|join(', ') }}), so the template headline is shown.</p>{% endif %}
</div>
</section>

<section id="patterns">
<h2>Patterns</h2>
<p class="sub">Counts exclude <code>unknown</code> unless stated. A row can have more than one auth method.</p>
<div class="grid2">
<div class="card"><h3>Which auth dominates</h3><div style="height:260px"><canvas id="c-auth"></canvas></div></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Self-serve vs gated</h3><div style="height:260px"><canvas id="c-ss"></canvas></div></div>
<div class="card" style="grid-column:1/-1"><h3>Self-serve vs gated, by category</h3><div style="height:300px"><canvas id="c-cat"></canvas></div></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Most common blockers</h3><div style="height:260px"><canvas id="c-block"></canvas></div></div>
<div class="card"><h3>MCP and Composio coverage</h3><div style="height:260px"><canvas id="c-mcp"></canvas></div></div>
</div>
<div class="grid2" style="margin-top:16px">
<div class="card"><h3>Easy wins ({{ patterns.easy_wins|length }})</h3><p class="small">Self-serve credentials, buildable, and not a Composio toolkit yet.</p>
<table><tr><th>App</th><th>Category</th><th>Access</th></tr>{% for r in patterns.easy_wins %}<tr><td>{{ r.app }}</td><td>{{ r.category }}</td><td>{{ r.self_serve }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td colspan="3">None found.</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Needs outreach ({{ patterns.needs_outreach|length }})</h3><p class="small">Partner, admin, or sales gate, or a partner/platform-review blocker.</p>
<table><tr><th>App</th><th>Category</th><th>Gate / blocker</th></tr>{% for r in patterns.needs_outreach %}<tr><td>{{ r.app }}</td><td>{{ r.category }}</td><td>{{ r.self_serve }} · {{ r.main_blocker }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td colspan="3">None found.</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
</div>
<details style="margin-top:16px" class="card"><summary>Category table</summary>
<table><tr><th>Category</th><th>Apps</th><th>Self-serve</th><th>Gated</th><th>Unknown</th><th>Buildable</th><th>In Composio</th></tr>
{% for c in patterns.by_category %}<tr><td>{{ c.category }}</td><td>{{ c.apps }}</td><td>{{ c.self_serve_open }}</td><td>{{ c.gated }}</td><td>{{ c.unknown }}</td><td>{{ c.buildable }}</td><td>{{ c.in_composio }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></details>
</section>

<section id="matrix">
<h2>The matrix: all {{ n }} apps</h2>
<p class="sub">Search or sort any column. Links under a cell are the docs pages quoted for it. <span class="pill human">human override</span> = a human confirmed the official domain. <span class="pill warn">needs human</span> = loops could not settle a field.</p>
<div class="card" style="overflow:auto">
<table id="matrix-table" class="display compact">
<thead><tr><th>App</th><th>Category</th><th>Auth</th><th>Access</th><th>REST / GraphQL</th><th>MCP</th><th>In Composio</th><th>Buildable</th><th>Blocker</th><th>Flags</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% macro evl(r, f) %}{% for e in r.ev.get(f, [])[:2] %}<a href="{{ e.url }}" title="{{ e.quote }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[{{ loop.index }}]</a>{% endfor %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro vp(v) %}{% set cls = 'unk' if v in ['unknown', None] else ('ok' if v in ['yes','self_serve_free','self_serve_trial','official','none'] else ('bad' if v in ['no','partner_gated','contact_sales','no_public_api'] else 'brand')) %}<span class="pill {{ cls }}">{{ v }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% for r in records %}
<tr>
<td><b>{{ r.app }}</b><div class="small">{{ r.one_liner }}</div></td>
<td>{{ r.category }}</td>
<td>{% for a in r.auth_methods %}{{ vp(a) }} {% endfor %}<div class="ev">{{ evl(r,'auth_methods') }}</div></td>
<td>{{ vp(r.self_serve) }}{% if r.gate_type not in ['none','unknown'] %}<div class="small">{{ r.gate_type }}</div>{% endif %}<div class="ev">{{ evl(r,'self_serve') }}{{ evl(r,'gate_type') }}</div></td>
<td>{{ r.api_surface.rest }} / {{ r.api_surface.graphql }}<div class="ev">{{ evl(r,'api_surface') }}</div></td>
<td>{{ vp(r.existing_mcp) }}{% if r.mcp_url %}<div class="ev"><a href="{{ r.mcp_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">link</a></div>{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ vp(r.composio_has_toolkit) }}{% if r.composio_slug %}<div class="small mono">{{ r.composio_slug }}</div>{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ vp(r.buildability) }}{% if r.derived %} <span class="pill unk" title="Derived by the fixed rule from evidenced access and API fields">rule</span>{% endif %}<div class="ev">{{ evl(r,'buildability') }}</div></td>
<td>{{ r.main_blocker }}{% if r.blocker_detail and r.blocker_detail != 'unknown' %}<div class="small">{{ r.blocker_detail }}</div>{% endif %}</td>
<td>{% if r.human_override %}<span class="pill human">human override</span> {% endif %}{% if r.needs_human %}<span class="pill warn" title="{{ r.needs_human_reasons|join('; ') }}">needs human</span>{% endif %}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
</section>

<section id="agent">
<h2>The agent</h2>
<p class="sub">A LangGraph pipeline per app. The orchestrator fans out over the 100 apps; each app runs the same subgraph.</p>
<div class="grid2">
<div class="card"><pre class="mermaid">
flowchart TD
  A[App name + hint] --> B{Domain override?}
  B -- human confirmed --> C[Seed official URLs]
  B -- no --> D[Search via Composio Tavily toolkit<br/>fallback: direct Tavily]
  C --> E[Official-domain filter]
  D --> E
  E --> F[Fetch to markdown cache]
  F --> G[Extract: Gemini, strict schema,<br/>URL + verbatim quote per field]
  G --> H[Pass 1 result]
  G --> V{Verify}
  V --> V1[Quote appears on page?]
  V --> V2[Composio toolkit API oracle]
  V --> V3[MCP registry lookup]
  V --> V4[Second model, other family]
  V1 & V2 & V3 & V4 --> W{Field failing?}
  W -- yes, loops < 2 --> R[Re-search only failing fields] --> G
  W -- no --> P[Pass 2 result]
  W -- still failing --> NH[needs_human flag]
</pre></div>
<div class="card">
<h3>What each piece does</h3>
<table>
<tr><td><b>Search</b></td><td>Composio's Tavily toolkit through the Composio SDK (<code>tools.execute</code>), falling back per call to direct Tavily.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Domain filter</b></td><td>Only pages on the app's official domain (or a human-confirmed one) are read. Third-party blogs are dropped.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Extract</b></td><td>{{ (stats[1] or {}).get('usage', {}).get('models', {}).keys()|list|join(', ') or 'Gemini flash-lite' }}. Strict JSON schema; a value without a quote found on the page is reset to unknown.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Oracle</b></td><td>Composio's own toolkit metadata (auth modes, managed auth) is ground truth for <i>composio_has_toolkit</i> and flags auth disagreements.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>MCP registry</b></td><td>registry.modelcontextprotocol.io search for existing servers.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Second model</b></td><td>Groq <code>openai/gpt-oss-120b</code> judges each claim against the quoted pages: supported, contradicted, or insufficient.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Loops</b></td><td>Only failing fields are re-searched and re-extracted, max 2 loops; anything still failing gets <i>needs_human</i>.</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>Run cost and time</h3>
<table><tr><th>Pass</th><th>Apps</th><th>Wall clock</th><th>LLM calls</th><th>Est. LLM cost</th></tr>
{% for p in [1,2,3] %}{% set s = stats[p] %}{% if s %}<tr><td>{{ p }}</td><td>{{ s.apps }}</td><td>{{ (s.wall_clock_s/60)|round(1) }} min</td><td>{{ s.usage.models.values()|map(attribute='calls')|sum }}</td><td>${{ '%.2f'|format(s.usage.cost_usd_known) }}</td></tr>{% endif %}{% else %}{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="small">Cost is tokens × published list price per 1M tokens; on a free tier the bill may be $0. Search credits (Tavily) are not included.</p>
</div></div>
<div class="card" style="margin-top:16px"><h3>Where the agent stops and a human decides</h3>
<p class="small">These handoffs happen on every run. Counts are measured from this run's data.</p>
<div style="overflow:auto"><table><tr><th>Handoff</th><th>This run</th><th>Trigger (in the code)</th><th>Human decides</th><th>Edits</th><th>Flows back via</th></tr>
{% for h in handoffs %}<tr><td><b>{{ h.name }}</b></td><td><b data-count="{{ h.key }}">{{ h.count }}</b> <span class="small">{{ h.count_label|safe }}</span></td><td class="small">{{ h.trigger|safe }}</td><td class="small">{{ h.decides }}</td><td class="small">{{ h.edits|safe }}</td><td class="small">{{ h.flows_back|safe }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
<p class="small"><b>One-time setup</b> (not part of each run): {{ one_time_setup|safe }}</p></div>
</section>

{% if pass3 %}<section id="pass3">
<h2>Pass 3: fewer unknowns, same evidence rule</h2>
<p class="sub">Pass 2's verifiers left many cells <code>unknown</code>. Pass 3 asks which of those unknowns had evidence all along, and finds new evidence without web search.</p>
<div class="grid2">
<div class="card"><h3>Unknown cells: Pass 1 → pass 2 → pass 3</h3>
<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Pass 1</th><th>Pass 2</th><th>Pass 3</th></tr>
{% for r in pass3.rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.field }}</td><td>{{ r.p1 }}</td><td>{{ r.p2 }}</td><td><b>{{ r.p3 }}</b></td></tr>{% endfor %}</table>
<p class="small">Out of {{ n }} apps. This is coverage, not accuracy.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>What filled the cells</h3>
<table><tr><th>Step</th><th>Fields</th></tr>{% for k, v in pass3.steps.items() %}<tr><td class="mono">{{ k }}</td><td>{{ v }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table>
<h3>Confidence tags on filled cells</h3>
<table><tr><th>Tag</th><th>Cells</th></tr>{% for k, v in pass3.tags.items() %}<tr><td class="mono">{{ k }}</td><td>{{ v }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
</div>
<div class="card" style="margin-top:16px"><h3>What changed and why</h3><ul>
<li><b>Policy fix.</b> In pass 2, a second model that said <i>insufficient</i> sent the field back for re-extraction, and the re-extraction often came back empty, so a claim with a verbatim quote from the official page was lost. Only <b>contradicted</b> demotes a claim now. A claim whose exact quote is found again on the cached official page is kept and tagged <code>quote-verified</code>. If the second model agreed, it's tagged <code>verifier-supported</code>. The second model's verdict is stored per field (<code>verifier_verdicts</code>).</li>
<li><b>Why pass 2's unknowns rose.</b> {{ pass3.crashed }} apps crashed in pass 2 when the model's daily quota ran out, leaving every field empty. That is the main reason pass 2 shows more unknowns than pass 1.</li>
<li><b>Pass 2 crashes.</b> Pass 3 restored their pass-1 claims only where the quote is still on the page. These rows stay <i>needs human</i>, because no second model checked them.</li>
<li><b>Composio metadata.</b> Every app was looked up in Composio's toolkit API by slug and by exact name. That sets <code>composio_has_toolkit</code> for all apps. For covered apps, the toolkit's auth schemes fill <code>auth_methods</code>, tagged <code>composio_metadata</code>. That tag means what Composio supports, which may be a subset of what the vendor offers.</li>
<li><b>Re-research without search.</b> For fields still unknown, common doc paths (/docs, /api, /developers, /authentication, /pricing, …) were fetched on the official host only. A model then extracted just those fields with strict verbatim quotes, and the quote had to be found on the page. Every model was quota-limited tonight, so the second-model check often did not run or could not decide. {{ pass3.research_claims - pass3.research_supported }} of {{ pass3.research_claims }} re-research claims are quote-verified only; {{ pass3.research_supported }} were confirmed by a second model. Across all of pass 3, {{ pass3.quote_only }} filled cells are quote-verified only and {{ pass3.supported_total }} are verifier-supported. A contradicted claim is dropped.</li>
<li><b>Rule verdicts.</b> buildability and main_blocker are still derived by the fixed rule from the evidenced fields (<code>derived_rule</code>). No value is filled by default. A cell with no evidence stays <code>unknown</code>.</li>
</ul></div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section id="try">
<h2>Try it: research a new company</h2>
<p class="sub">The same graph runs for one app by name or URL and can append it to the dataset.</p>
<div class="grid3">
<div class="card"><h3>From the terminal</h3><pre>pip install -e .
python -m opsresearch research-one "Notion" 
python -m opsresearch research-one "https://acme.dev" --append</pre></div>
<div class="card"><h3>From GitHub (no setup)</h3><p>Run the <a href="{{ repo_url }}/actions/workflows/research-one.yml">research-one workflow</a> with a name or URL. It researches the app, appends it to <code>results.json</code>, re-renders this page and redeploys.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>From an agent (MCP)</h3><pre>{"mcpServers":{"composio-apps":{
 "command":"python",
 "args":["-m","opsresearch.mcp_server"]}}}</pre><p class="small">Tools: query_apps, get_app, patterns, research_one.</p></div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="honesty">
<h2>Honesty and limitations</h2>
<div class="grid2">
<div class="card"><ul>
<li><b>Unknown is an answer.</b> A field without a verbatim quote from an official page is <code>unknown</code>, not a guess. Unknown counts are shown in every chart and table.</li>
<li><b>Human-touched rows are marked.</b> {{ overrides|length }} rows used a human-confirmed domain ({% for r in overrides %}{{ r.app }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}). No answer was hand-edited into the agent output.</li>
<li><b>Accuracy is not claimed on this page.</b> Agreement with a 20-app gold sample is reported in the README (Verification).{% if gold_by_ai %} Those labels were drafted by an AI model from official docs, independently of this pipeline{% if gold_reviewed %}, and reviewed and confirmed by a human.{% else %}, and human review is pending.{% endif %}{% endif %}</li>
<li><b>Gated is a finding.</b> Partner-only or contact-sales APIs are reported as such when a page says so.</li>
</ul></div>
<div class="card"><ul>
<li><b>Model availability changed the plan.</b> The planned Gemini 2.5 Flash was withdrawn for new keys on the day. Extraction ran on free-tier Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite (15 requests a minute), with 3.1 Flash-Lite as fallback when it was overloaded. These are smaller models.</li>
<li><b>Search credits ran out mid-build.</b> Tavily's free 1,000 monthly credits (shared by the Composio Tavily toolkit and the direct fallback) were used up by the early runs. The final runs reused the official pages already fetched and cached, and re-research could only probe common doc paths. Fresh credits would let the loops find more new pages.</li>
<li><b>Verdicts by rule.</b> {{ derived_count }} buildability verdicts were derived by a fixed rule from evidenced access and API fields (tagged "rule"), not quoted from a page.</li>
<li><b>Docs behind JS or logins</b> are thin to a plain HTTP fetch, so those apps lean to unknown.</li>
<li><b>API breadth is kept in the data but left off the page:</b> it is hard to judge consistently from docs and agreed with the gold labels on only 1 of 20 apps.</li>
<li><b>The second model can be wrong too.</b> It flags disagreement; it is not ground truth. Composio's API is ground truth only for Composio coverage.</li>
<li><b>Point in time.</b> Docs were cached on {{ generated[:10] }}; pages change.</li>
</ul></div></div>
</section>

